 # Python Environment Management

This rule provides guidelines for managing Python virtual environments in the project.

## Virtual Environment Setup and Usage

- Location: `.venv` directory
- Python Version: 3.11.x (do not use Python 3.13 due to dependency compatibility)
- Activation: `source .venv/bin/activate`

## Important Commands
Always use full paths due to shell aliases:

- Python execution: `.venv/bin/python`
- Version check: `.venv/bin/python --version`
- Install dependencies: `.venv/bin/pip install -r requirements.txt`
- Running tools: `.venv/bin/python -c "import tools; ..."`

## Key Requirements
- Verify Python version shows 3.11.x before proceeding
- Always use the virtual environment for all Python operations
- Install all dependencies within the virtual environment